 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 507816,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Write an application that can be solved using the equation <span data-math=\"25x + 75 = 200\">25x + 75 = 200</span>. Then solve your application.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The application you write will vary.</p>\n<p>Then, solve the algebraic equation: <span data-math=\"25x + 75 = 200\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 1: Simplify each side as much as possible.</p>\n<p>This is already done.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"25x + 75 = 200\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: Collect the variable terms on one side.</p>\n<p>This is already done.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"25x + 75 = 200\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 3: Collect the constant terms on the other side.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"25x + 75 - 75 = 200 - 75\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"25x = 125\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 4: Make the coefficient of the variable term equal to 1.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{25x}}{{25}} = \\frac{{125}}{{25}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"x = 5\"></span></p>\n<p>Write a sentence that uses the 5 regarding your application.</p>\n<p>Step 5: Checking is left to you.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Answers will vary. For example: You can rent a paddleboard for $25 per hour with a water shoe purchase of $75. If you spent $200, how many hours did you rent the paddle board for?<br>\nYou rented the paddle board for 5 hours.\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
